  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1220 PM CDT Sun Jun 28 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will continue to amplify and be centered\nover Middle TN through at least the middle part of the week. This\nwill bring a prolonged period of very hot temperatures. Highs\nthrough at least Friday will be in the mid to upper 90s and\nafternoon heat index values will be as hot as 110. There will be\nlimited relief from the heat overnight as lows will only fall into\nthe mid to upper 70s. This heat and duration will bring extreme\nheat risk to much of Middle TN by Tuesday and will remain extreme at\nleast through Friday. Extreme Heat Risk means that there is rare \nand or long duration extreme heat with little to no overnight \nrelief affecting anyone without cooling/hydration as well as \nhealth systems, industries, and infrastructure. \n\nThe upper level ridge will drift east late week and start to \nbreak down some next weekend. That will bring some cooling for the\n4th of July weekend but it will be limited. Highs will still \nremain in the low to mid 90s with afternoon heat index values in \nthe triple digits. With the upper level ridge just to our east we \nwill see low chances for pop up afternoon/evening thunderstorms \nFriday into the weekend.",
